# Histidine, 12-qubit NMR molecule
# Reference [20]: Negrevergne et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 96, 170501 (2006)
#
# Nuclei (12) — 13C/15N-labeled histidine (imidazole side chain):
#   0 = N1   (backbone alpha-amino N)
#   1 = Ca   (alpha carbon)
#   2 = Cb   (beta carbon, CH2)
#   3 = Cg   (gamma, imidazole C)
#   4 = Cd2  (imidazole C)
#   5 = Ne2  (imidazole N)
#   6 = Ce1  (imidazole C)
#   7 = Nd1  (imidazole N)
#   8 = C    (carbonyl carbon)
#   9 = Ha   (alpha H)
#  10 = Hb1  (beta H)
#  11 = Hb2  (beta H)
#
# Approximate J-coupling values (Hz):
#   1J C-C  ≈ 35-55 Hz → W ≈ 45-71
#   1J C-N  ≈  8-12 Hz → W ≈ 208-312
#   1J C-H  ≈ 130-150 Hz → W ≈ 17-19
#   2J C-C  ≈   2-5 Hz → W ≈ 500-1250
#   3J H-H  ≈   3-7 Hz → W ≈ 357-833
#
# NOTE: values are approximate; exact coupling matrix from [20] required for
#       precise Table II/III reproduction.
12
